WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.173 --> 00:00:02.006
- What's up Believe Nation.

00:00:02.006 --> 00:00:02.955
Today I'm going to share with you

00:00:02.955 --> 00:00:05.095
my Favorite Top 10 Rules for Success,

00:00:05.095 --> 00:00:06.678
April 2017 edition.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.829
And as always guys, as people are talking,

00:00:09.829 --> 00:00:11.472
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:11.472 --> 00:00:13.408
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:13.408 --> 00:00:14.888
put quotes around it as
well, so other people

00:00:14.888 --> 00:00:17.314
can be inspired, and when
you write something down,

00:00:17.314 --> 00:00:20.195
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself as well.

00:00:20.195 --> 00:00:21.028
Enjoy.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.590
- Go hard, and then when
you think you're going hard,

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.643
go harder, like that's
really it, just hustle.

00:00:31.643 --> 00:00:32.633
You know what I mean?

00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:35.715
There's nothing in life that
you can't put enough work in

00:00:35.715 --> 00:00:38.821
every single day and not get better at,

00:00:38.821 --> 00:00:40.390
you know what I mean?

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:43.395
If you want to be good at
something, you know what I mean?

00:00:43.395 --> 00:00:46.104
Like you can't just like
not like do it every day

00:00:46.104 --> 00:00:47.427
and not get better.

00:00:47.427 --> 00:00:48.625
It's the same shit with music.

00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:49.815
It's the same shit with learning

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:51.009
how to play an instrument or something.

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:53.067
If you spend your time
practicing your craft,

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:55.568
like, you know, that's
really it, it's just,

00:00:55.568 --> 00:00:58.937
you know, because now days
it's like with the Internet,

00:00:58.937 --> 00:01:01.853
everything is so accessible and, you know,

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:05.543
everybody in the world is a
rapper, you know what I mean?

00:01:05.543 --> 00:01:07.351
Everybody's putting music out,

00:01:07.351 --> 00:01:09.203
so it's like how do you stand out?

00:01:09.203 --> 00:01:10.725
Quality is always going to matter,

00:01:10.725 --> 00:01:12.246
but also being different.

00:01:12.246 --> 00:01:14.304
You can't try to be different,
you know what I mean?

00:01:14.304 --> 00:01:16.032
But you just got to be yourself.

00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:17.878
- [Interviewer] What's the
biggest risk you've taken

00:01:17.878 --> 00:01:19.686
that you feel has paid off?

00:01:19.686 --> 00:01:23.686
- The biggest risk I've
taken that has paid off.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.013
I'd have to say Cookie.

00:01:27.013 --> 00:01:31.180
I mean, I was very nervous
when I received the script.

00:01:32.853 --> 00:01:35.158
She wasn't the most likable character,

00:01:35.158 --> 00:01:37.135
and I've played some
pretty edgy characters,

00:01:37.135 --> 00:01:40.135
but this one was particularly a challenge

00:01:40.135 --> 00:01:41.911
because it was prime
time network television,

00:01:41.911 --> 00:01:46.265
and I wasn't sure how
people would receive her.

00:01:46.265 --> 00:01:48.565
I mean, she beat her son with a broom,

00:01:48.565 --> 00:01:50.815
even though he deserved it.

00:01:51.973 --> 00:01:53.580
She called one son a fagot.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.580
I mean, it was scary, but
I'm the type of artist

00:01:59.546 --> 00:02:03.330
that if the role doesn't
scare me, I don't want it,

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.931
because it's not going
to change me as a person.

00:02:05.931 --> 00:02:10.373
So I took a risk, and that's
what you do as artists.

00:02:10.373 --> 00:02:13.611
You jump in feet first
and you see where it goes.

00:02:13.611 --> 00:02:17.150
And I knew that we had something special.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.928
I don't just jump feet
first for any project.

00:02:20.928 --> 00:02:23.153
I knew this was something special.

00:02:23.153 --> 00:02:25.659
I knew that what Fox was trying to do,

00:02:25.659 --> 00:02:27.596
what Lee Daniels and Danny
Strong were trying to do,

00:02:27.596 --> 00:02:29.776
and what I was trying to do,

00:02:29.776 --> 00:02:31.333
was shake up television.

00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:34.494
It's too safe.
Life is not safe.

00:02:34.494 --> 00:02:37.665
I think we did that with this show.

00:02:37.665 --> 00:02:40.993
So I'm so proud to be
a part of this project,

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:42.966
and I'm so proud that Fox believed in us

00:02:42.966 --> 00:02:44.200
and took a chance,

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.059
because that's what
art is about, isn't it?

00:02:46.059 --> 00:02:49.835
Taking chances, taking risks (laughs).

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:51.814
- I think if you don't actually
believe what you're doing,

00:02:51.814 --> 00:02:55.354
it's really important if you
don't derive satisfaction

00:02:55.354 --> 00:02:58.478
from what you're doing,
then you will not be able

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.818
to sustain all of the
bad things that happen

00:03:00.818 --> 00:03:02.540
in the incredibly long period of time

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.349
that the bad things happen over.

00:03:04.349 --> 00:03:07.968
And so, the only motivation
that I have seen work for people

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:11.794
over a long period of time is enjoyment

00:03:11.794 --> 00:03:14.098
in what they're doing
and an intense believe

00:03:14.098 --> 00:03:15.993
that it matters, and
ideally liking the people

00:03:15.993 --> 00:03:17.971
that they go to work with every day.

00:03:17.971 --> 00:03:21.919
But the, I think the reasons
that a lot of people,

00:03:21.919 --> 00:03:23.400
and by the way, it's
totally cool when people

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.496
start off saying well I want to make money

00:03:25.496 --> 00:03:26.813
or I want to be famous.

00:03:26.813 --> 00:03:28.129
I think a lot of people start that way,

00:03:28.129 --> 00:03:29.449
and they don't like to admit it,

00:03:29.449 --> 00:03:32.328
but pretty quickly, or at
least in the first few years,

00:03:32.328 --> 00:03:35.164
I think a lot of people
find a deeper mission

00:03:35.164 --> 00:03:37.668
for why they do what they do,
and that that drives them then

00:03:37.668 --> 00:03:40.339
for the rest of the time they work.

00:03:40.339 --> 00:03:43.669
- I look around at my
girlfriends and my guy friends,

00:03:43.669 --> 00:03:46.422
and they're in jobs that
they don't really have a lot

00:03:46.422 --> 00:03:49.675
of growth potential in, that
they're not passionate about,

00:03:49.675 --> 00:03:51.605
and I think if we're ever
going to make bold decisions,

00:03:51.605 --> 00:03:53.411
it has to be at this point in our life.

00:03:53.411 --> 00:03:54.644
You know, we have to be out there,

00:03:54.644 --> 00:03:56.868
we have to be experimenting,
we have to be looking

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:59.703
for that which makes us tick,
and I think a big part of that

00:03:59.703 --> 00:04:03.870
evolution for me was really
summer jobs and working

00:04:04.958 --> 00:04:07.637
and making sure to
actually get into the world

00:04:07.637 --> 00:04:10.024
and try different things
and eliminate those,

00:04:10.024 --> 00:04:12.574
which is as useful,
eliminating those career paths

00:04:12.574 --> 00:04:14.550
that you're not interested in as it is

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:18.129
doing things that do interest you.

00:04:18.129 --> 00:04:21.458
But I think just being
bold and taking risks

00:04:21.458 --> 00:04:23.228
when you're young is so important

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:26.398
because I can't imagine
working the hours that I do

00:04:26.398 --> 00:04:28.455
if I didn't fundamentally love it.

00:04:28.455 --> 00:04:29.647
And I think that's the difference

00:04:29.647 --> 00:04:31.987
between somebody whose successful

00:04:31.987 --> 00:04:33.973
and somebody that's extremely successful.

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:36.974
Somebody that's good and somebody
that's exceptionally good.

00:04:36.974 --> 00:04:41.141
Is the level of drive, which
directly stems from passion.

00:04:42.072 --> 00:04:43.472
- There's different types
of people in this world,

00:04:43.472 --> 00:04:45.943
and one thing that we're
all going to deal with

00:04:45.943 --> 00:04:48.609
is like difficulties in our tasks

00:04:48.609 --> 00:04:50.585
trying to become successful.

00:04:50.585 --> 00:04:53.706
As good as things get,
you're going to have

00:04:53.706 --> 00:04:55.557
the same amount of bad
that's going to try to impede

00:04:55.557 --> 00:04:57.619
your progress, whether it be people,

00:04:57.619 --> 00:05:00.130
whether it be the IRS,
whether it be whatever.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:04.569
Something will rear its ugly
head and try to block you.

00:05:04.569 --> 00:05:07.945
Now, a lot of people
can't handle that shit.

00:05:07.945 --> 00:05:11.933
When you have a vision
and something or someone

00:05:11.933 --> 00:05:14.159
throws a curve ball, it hurts.

00:05:14.159 --> 00:05:15.799
It stings, right?

00:05:15.799 --> 00:05:19.172
It's like your baby and
now I can't put my baby

00:05:19.172 --> 00:05:21.068
out there like I want to do it,

00:05:21.068 --> 00:05:22.880
so it really throws people off.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:23.990
They get really negative.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.138
They may get depressed.

00:05:25.138 --> 00:05:26.083
They might want to stop.

00:05:26.083 --> 00:05:27.481
They might just want to
back to their nine to five.

00:05:27.481 --> 00:05:28.840
That's fine.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.933
It's not for everybody to push through.

00:05:30.933 --> 00:05:32.451
But for those who can push through,

00:05:32.451 --> 00:05:34.382
like you said, the
difference between those

00:05:34.382 --> 00:05:36.235
who really succeed and those who don't

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:40.261
are the ones who, when
they're faced with whatever

00:05:40.261 --> 00:05:41.948
these difficulties are,

00:05:41.948 --> 00:05:44.050
they're like I'm going
to keep pushing through.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:45.573
I'm going to keep pushing through.

00:05:45.573 --> 00:05:47.952
Because, it sounds corny and cliche,

00:05:47.952 --> 00:05:50.008
but there's always
sunshine after the rain.

00:05:50.008 --> 00:05:51.242
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:51.242 --> 00:05:52.928
Rain don't last that long.

00:05:52.928 --> 00:05:54.863
You got to know that and be aware of that.

00:05:54.863 --> 00:05:56.181
That's something you can take with you

00:05:56.181 --> 00:05:58.028
through everything in
life, but in business,

00:05:58.028 --> 00:06:00.333
you cannot stop because
things are not going right

00:06:00.333 --> 00:06:02.758
at the time, because it's going to happen.

00:06:02.758 --> 00:06:04.038
I've dealt with it.

00:06:04.038 --> 00:06:06.135
I'm sure I'll deal with
it again at some point.

00:06:06.135 --> 00:06:08.234
- The number one thing that's
going to change your life.

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.990
The only thing that will change your life,

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:12.761
change your business, change your money,

00:06:12.761 --> 00:06:16.928
change your relationship, is
you must raise your standard.

00:06:18.476 --> 00:06:21.893
I know that sounds boring, stupid, basic,

00:06:23.254 --> 00:06:25.514
but it's the truth.

00:06:25.514 --> 00:06:27.988
The only thing that
changes our life long term

00:06:27.988 --> 00:06:30.664
is when we raise our standards.

00:06:30.664 --> 00:06:32.722
What does that mean?

00:06:32.722 --> 00:06:35.435
That sounds so boring and dumb.

00:06:35.435 --> 00:06:39.602
It means that all of us in
life have things we want.

00:06:41.322 --> 00:06:45.489
We don't get what we want;
we get what we have to have.

00:06:46.466 --> 00:06:50.783
Remember I said earlier, we
all get what we tolerate.

00:06:50.783 --> 00:06:53.036
In ourselves, in other people.

00:06:53.036 --> 00:06:55.792
But when you're no longer
willing to tolerate something,

00:06:55.792 --> 00:06:58.292
that's when your life changes.

00:06:59.331 --> 00:07:03.277
The difference in people
is their standards, period.

00:07:03.277 --> 00:07:06.937
The difference in people
is their standards, period.

00:07:06.937 --> 00:07:09.406
And what do I mean by standards?

00:07:09.406 --> 00:07:13.017
Every one in the world
has a list of things

00:07:13.017 --> 00:07:15.184
they think they should do.

00:07:16.185 --> 00:07:17.706
I should lose weight.

00:07:17.706 --> 00:07:19.393
I should work out.

00:07:19.393 --> 00:07:21.862
I should spend more time with my kids.

00:07:21.862 --> 00:07:23.757
I should work harder.

00:07:23.757 --> 00:07:25.154
I should make more calls.

00:07:25.154 --> 00:07:28.606
I should, I should, I should, I should.

00:07:28.606 --> 00:07:30.085
And then you know what?

00:07:30.085 --> 00:07:31.529
People don't do their shoulds,

00:07:31.529 --> 00:07:32.929
and they get mad at themselves,

00:07:32.929 --> 00:07:34.737
and they, what I call,
should all over themselves.

00:07:34.737 --> 00:07:37.120
They beat themselves up about it.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:41.287
What changes people is when
your should becomes a must.

00:07:42.304 --> 00:07:45.181
When suddenly the thing
you said should happen,

00:07:45.181 --> 00:07:46.781
has to happen.

00:07:46.781 --> 00:07:49.209
That's when human beings change.

00:07:49.209 --> 00:07:51.968
It's like if you want to take the island,

00:07:51.968 --> 00:07:53.324
and you're the head of the army

00:07:53.324 --> 00:07:54.765
and you want to take the island,

00:07:54.765 --> 00:07:57.439
the most powerful way to take
the island is burn the boats.

00:07:57.439 --> 00:07:59.456
Because if there's no way to go back,

00:07:59.456 --> 00:08:01.923
it's amazing what happens when it's a must

00:08:01.923 --> 00:08:04.474
to do something versus a should.

00:08:04.474 --> 00:08:07.031
That's what makes human beings succeed.

00:08:07.031 --> 00:08:09.208
- If you want to be a
fireman, go and do it.

00:08:09.208 --> 00:08:10.527
If you want to be a ballet dancer,

00:08:10.527 --> 00:08:11.678
then go and be a ballet dancer.

00:08:11.678 --> 00:08:12.908
If you don't believe in yourself,

00:08:12.908 --> 00:08:14.431
then no one else will believe in you.

00:08:14.431 --> 00:08:17.851
It's an important, it's
so important for me

00:08:17.851 --> 00:08:20.813
to people to understand that
I want to be an inspiration.

00:08:20.813 --> 00:08:24.678
I was unique, as kind of
nine out of 10 children are,

00:08:24.678 --> 00:08:26.733
and I wanted to be a role
model, and I think now

00:08:26.733 --> 00:08:28.535
I'm in the kind of
limelight to go it's okay

00:08:28.535 --> 00:08:31.417
and it's the special people that believe,

00:08:31.417 --> 00:08:33.061
that ones that have something magical,

00:08:33.061 --> 00:08:35.566
and it's something that you
can turn into a positive

00:08:35.566 --> 00:08:37.586
and not let it eat you away.

00:08:37.586 --> 00:08:39.679
There'll always be someone
that says you can't do it.

00:08:39.679 --> 00:08:41.984
There'll always be someone that
says I don't believe in you.

00:08:41.984 --> 00:08:44.169
There'll always be someone
that says I do believe in you,

00:08:44.169 --> 00:08:46.137
and there's always someone
that says you can do it.

00:08:46.137 --> 00:08:47.994
And that's the people
that you have to focus on.

00:08:47.994 --> 00:08:49.883
However much people try to
put me down, which they do

00:08:49.883 --> 00:08:51.612
when they say, you know,
every time I hear your song

00:08:51.612 --> 00:08:55.756
I want to burn my ears,
I say whose laughing now.

00:08:55.756 --> 00:08:58.712
- What it finally comes
down to in your business

00:08:58.712 --> 00:09:02.907
and how you run it is
you first and me second.

00:09:02.907 --> 00:09:04.907
Take that home with you.

00:09:05.867 --> 00:09:08.341
You first and me second.

00:09:08.341 --> 00:09:11.385
The first thing you want to do
is help your people succeed,

00:09:11.385 --> 00:09:13.197
and then you succeed.

00:09:13.197 --> 00:09:15.089
Just keep it in the right order.

00:09:15.089 --> 00:09:16.905
It's not you succeeding and then hopefully

00:09:16.905 --> 00:09:18.488
they come out okay.

00:09:19.617 --> 00:09:22.652
It's all about them, not about you.

00:09:22.652 --> 00:09:25.620
And I think that was the
foundation of our business.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:29.202
We never, Jay and I never
talked about how much money

00:09:29.202 --> 00:09:32.370
we made or how much
money we wanted to make.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:35.248
We talked about how big we'd
like to have our business,

00:09:35.248 --> 00:09:39.569
but it was never a
personal financial goal.

00:09:39.569 --> 00:09:42.241
But our focus was on how
we could enrich the lives

00:09:42.241 --> 00:09:45.442
of our people and make them better.

00:09:45.442 --> 00:09:49.471
Often times influencing
them with our faith as well.

00:09:49.471 --> 00:09:53.129
- I feel a genuine need to
communicate with an audience,

00:09:53.129 --> 00:09:57.735
and it might just be the
attention I didn't get as a kid.

00:09:57.735 --> 00:10:01.023
It can't come from anything good.

00:10:01.023 --> 00:10:04.474
But what I try and do is
bring the best information

00:10:04.474 --> 00:10:07.474
I can to the stage and broadcast it.

00:10:08.628 --> 00:10:12.169
So it's reportage from distant points,

00:10:12.169 --> 00:10:16.252
from a fairly unique
standpoint, and so basically

00:10:17.227 --> 00:10:19.410
I'm not keeping it all to myself,

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:23.142
but I earnestly try to, it's
not about entertainment,

00:10:23.142 --> 00:10:26.001
it's about communication,
warning, broadcasting,

00:10:26.001 --> 00:10:30.084
emitting, and trying to
leave something of myself

00:10:32.184 --> 00:10:33.684
with the audience.

00:10:35.196 --> 00:10:36.593
It's not mere entertainment.

00:10:36.593 --> 00:10:38.567
It's not just making people laugh or not.

00:10:38.567 --> 00:10:40.150
It's got to hurt me.

00:10:41.737 --> 00:10:44.289
It's got to leave lines in my face.

00:10:44.289 --> 00:10:49.227
I don't like any artistic
endeavor that doesn't extol

00:10:49.227 --> 00:10:51.736
a price on the one doing it.

00:10:51.736 --> 00:10:54.668
So I'm not looking to get
through these things okay.

00:10:54.668 --> 00:10:56.478
These things are actually very difficult

00:10:56.478 --> 00:11:00.263
and very hard on my psyche,
which makes me think

00:11:00.263 --> 00:11:02.028
I'm doing the right thing.

00:11:02.028 --> 00:11:06.141
- Hublot came out with a product in 1980.

00:11:06.141 --> 00:11:08.651
A product that was based on an innovation

00:11:08.651 --> 00:11:11.234
to introduce rubber as a strap.

00:11:12.231 --> 00:11:16.470
It seems very common
today, but rubber in 1980

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:18.720
was a real courageous move.

00:11:23.583 --> 00:11:25.272
It was even the provocation.

00:11:25.272 --> 00:11:29.388
People say hey, on a gold watch, rubber?

00:11:29.388 --> 00:11:32.060
Because people didn't know
rubber comes from a tree,

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:36.710
rubber is natural, rubber
is very comfortable,

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:40.081
it's very flexible, and
rubber is very resistant,

00:11:40.081 --> 00:11:43.205
and it's waterproof, so
finally it's ideal for a watch,

00:11:43.205 --> 00:11:46.733
but in those days, people
thought it's a provocation,

00:11:46.733 --> 00:11:49.483
and then Hublot could not evolve.

00:11:51.556 --> 00:11:55.723
They stayed on the product, and
I said we are not a product.

00:11:59.421 --> 00:12:01.599
We have a message first.

00:12:01.599 --> 00:12:03.079
We have a concept.

00:12:03.079 --> 00:12:05.711
And the concept is fusion.

00:12:05.711 --> 00:12:07.114
Why?

00:12:07.114 --> 00:12:10.859
Because in 1980, when we put
gold together with rubber,

00:12:10.859 --> 00:12:13.782
we created a fusion
because gold and rubber

00:12:13.782 --> 00:12:15.433
never come together.

00:12:15.433 --> 00:12:18.931
They were together only one time in life,

00:12:18.931 --> 00:12:20.598
during The Big Bang.

00:12:22.124 --> 00:12:23.476
Then everything was in one.

00:12:23.476 --> 00:12:28.414
Then rubber went away and
said okay I go now on my tree,

00:12:28.414 --> 00:12:31.416
and gold said okay I go
and rest in South Africa

00:12:31.416 --> 00:12:33.801
under the earth, and
since then they never met,

00:12:33.801 --> 00:12:37.134
until people take them and connect them.

00:12:38.373 --> 00:12:41.134
So I said Hublot made a fusion.

00:12:41.134 --> 00:12:43.693
And fusion must be our message.

00:12:43.693 --> 00:12:45.456
Must be our philosophy.

00:12:45.456 --> 00:12:47.511
Must be our religion.

00:12:47.511 --> 00:12:50.021
And once we have this religion clear,

00:12:50.021 --> 00:12:51.938
and it is named fusion,

00:12:52.979 --> 00:12:56.349
then we can develop further products.

00:12:56.349 --> 00:12:59.601
Not necessarily need the rubber anymore

00:12:59.601 --> 00:13:03.676
because fusion goes further
way than just rubber.

00:13:03.676 --> 00:13:04.664
It can be carbon.

00:13:04.664 --> 00:13:07.621
It can be ceramic, whatever.

00:13:07.621 --> 00:13:11.621
So I was capable to free
Hublot from the product

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:17.532
and give Hublot a message,
and from that message,

00:13:17.532 --> 00:13:19.996
new products were born.

00:13:19.996 --> 00:13:23.246
And that was the most important element

00:13:24.811 --> 00:13:27.524
in the revival of the brand.

00:13:27.524 --> 00:13:31.107
It's to take it away
from a product concept

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:36.523
and to give it a brand message,

00:13:37.816 --> 00:13:39.758
and from the brand message

00:13:39.758 --> 00:13:43.258
were then later born in 2005 new products.

00:13:45.104 --> 00:13:49.271
- When you finish a film,
your job basically is over.

00:13:51.942 --> 00:13:55.025
You have a desire to share your work,

00:13:56.378 --> 00:13:59.734
and so you put it out into the world.

00:13:59.734 --> 00:14:03.478
You realize that yes you
can help the film some

00:14:03.478 --> 00:14:07.561
by giving interviews or
you can go to some places

00:14:09.526 --> 00:14:13.693
and have talks, but basically,
the film is on its own,

00:14:14.623 --> 00:14:16.476
and you can't tell whether
it's going to go good

00:14:16.476 --> 00:14:18.569
or going to go bad.

00:14:18.569 --> 00:14:21.039
It's important that you
believe in your work,

00:14:21.039 --> 00:14:24.039
and that's the most important thing.

00:14:26.426 --> 00:14:30.559
- I watched so many matches
in my life, unbelievable.

00:14:30.559 --> 00:14:34.051
And I really, there are some boring games,

00:14:34.051 --> 00:14:38.045
and then I sleep, and
it's so boring and I think

00:14:38.045 --> 00:14:42.177
why they meet each other
and make this 20, 40, 50,

00:14:42.177 --> 00:14:46.292
60, 70, 80,000 people in a
stadium for this boring game.

00:14:46.292 --> 00:14:47.435
It's not okay.

00:14:47.435 --> 00:14:49.224
So that's what we want to see.

00:14:49.224 --> 00:14:51.319
We want to enjoy our own game.

00:14:51.319 --> 00:14:54.159
If we lose, okay, we like to win,

00:14:54.159 --> 00:14:56.916
but if we lose, with our way it's okay.

00:14:56.916 --> 00:14:58.524
If we lose with the way of somebody else,

00:14:58.524 --> 00:15:03.176
it's, you cannot work
with this, so that's it.

00:15:03.176 --> 00:15:06.843
It's very emotional,
very fast, very strong,

00:15:07.981 --> 00:15:10.648
not boring, no chess, like this.

00:15:13.243 --> 00:15:17.939
Yes of course tactical yes
but tactical with big heart

00:15:17.939 --> 00:15:21.513
and tactical things are so important.

00:15:21.513 --> 00:15:23.773
You cannot win without tactical things,

00:15:23.773 --> 00:15:27.102
but the emotion makes the difference.

00:15:27.102 --> 00:15:30.433
Life in our game, that's important.

00:15:30.433 --> 00:15:33.716
- I remember I gave this talk
to a group of entrepreneurs,

00:15:33.716 --> 00:15:35.894
and this one woman raised
her hand, and she goes

00:15:35.894 --> 00:15:38.032
well, you're real positive,
but what do you do,

00:15:38.032 --> 00:15:40.457
what do you tell yourself
when you just wasted

00:15:40.457 --> 00:15:42.711
a year-and-a-half of
your life doing something

00:15:42.711 --> 00:15:44.435
and it didn't work out.

00:15:44.435 --> 00:15:49.126
And I told her, that's a real
negative way of looking at it.

00:15:49.126 --> 00:15:52.992
Can you rephrase the question
and then ask me again.

00:15:52.992 --> 00:15:54.924
Because you're looking
at it really negatively,

00:15:54.924 --> 00:15:57.101
first of all, so I didn't even
want to answer it that way.

00:15:57.101 --> 00:15:58.826
So she thought about it, and she said,

00:15:58.826 --> 00:16:01.461
well I learned an important
lesson the hard way.

00:16:01.461 --> 00:16:03.271
I said, that still sucks.

00:16:03.271 --> 00:16:05.457
No wonder you don't want to move forward,

00:16:05.457 --> 00:16:07.673
because you feel like
you've done something wrong

00:16:07.673 --> 00:16:09.773
because it didn't work out
the way you had predetermined

00:16:09.773 --> 00:16:11.784
you wanted it to work out.

00:16:11.784 --> 00:16:13.345
You have to look at it a different way.

00:16:13.345 --> 00:16:14.825
If you feel like you want to do something,

00:16:14.825 --> 00:16:16.059
you should just step forward.

00:16:16.059 --> 00:16:18.975
It may not work, but
you're going to hit a step

00:16:18.975 --> 00:16:21.194
in your career and in your development

00:16:21.194 --> 00:16:23.999
that you could not have taken
had you not gone that way

00:16:23.999 --> 00:16:25.441
before you can get over there.

00:16:25.441 --> 00:16:27.455
And I say in the ashes
of all your failures,

00:16:27.455 --> 00:16:30.382
if you look close enough,
you'll find keys to success.

00:16:30.382 --> 00:16:31.741
If you're a very negative person,

00:16:31.741 --> 00:16:34.535
all you would focus on is
wow I have a really bad movie

00:16:34.535 --> 00:16:37.246
on my resume that I wish I had never done.

00:16:37.246 --> 00:16:39.547
But if you're a positive
person, you'll go I'm so glad

00:16:39.547 --> 00:16:42.590
I took that step that most
people would not have taken

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:46.209
because that got me to a place
that no one else can follow.

00:16:46.209 --> 00:16:47.404
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:16:47.404 --> 00:16:48.803
I'd love to know what did you think,

00:16:48.803 --> 00:16:50.448
what was your favorite clip,
what are you going to take

00:16:50.448 --> 00:16:52.541
from this video and
immediately apply to your life

00:16:52.541 --> 00:16:53.983
or your business somehow.

00:16:53.983 --> 00:16:55.380
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:56.738
I'm super curious to find out.

00:16:56.738 --> 00:16:58.750
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Riza Pereira.

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:00.965
Thank you so much Riza for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:17:00.965 --> 00:17:02.249
"Your One Word".

00:17:02.249 --> 00:17:04.123
It really, really really
means a lot to me,

00:17:04.123 --> 00:17:05.686
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:17:05.686 --> 00:17:07.083
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:17:07.083 --> 00:17:08.231
I believe in you.

00:17:08.231 --> 00:17:09.922
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:17:09.922 --> 00:17:12.263
and whatever your one word is.

00:17:12.263 --> 00:17:14.680
Much love, I'll see you soon.

